class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them. In 2025, on the county&rsquo;s middle value, August to September came in at 55% of normal and April to May at 64%, while June to July ran 153%. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, and grid 24450 got just 51% of normal that year.</p>"}
